    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n212.jpg">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="8" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/genesis_8_1/genesis_8"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/genesis_8_1/genesis_8/1" n="1"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/8/1">‘God remembered Noah and all the beasts and all the cattle that were with him in the ark, and God caused a wind to pass over the earth and the waters subsided’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And it was said:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="2" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/exodus_2_24/exodus_2"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/exodus_2_24/exodus_2/24" n="24"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:exodus/2/24">‘God heard their cry, then God remembered His covenant with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And it was said:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="26" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/leviticus_26_42/leviticus_26"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/leviticus_26_42/leviticus_26/42" n="42"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:leviticus/26/42">‘I will remember my covenant with Jacob, as well as my covenant with Isaac and my covenant with Abraham will I also remember, and the land will I remember.’</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And in Thy holy words it is written:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="111" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/psalms_111_4/psalms_111"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/psalms_111_4/psalms_111/4" n="4"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/111/4">‘A memorial has He made for His wonders, gracious and compassionate is the Lord’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And it was said:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="111" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/psalms_111_5/psalms_111"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/psalms_111_5/psalms_111/5" n="5"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/111/5">‘He gave food to those that fear Him, He will remember His covenant for ever’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And it was said:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="106" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/psalms_106_45/psalms_106"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/psalms_106_45/psalms_106/45" n="45"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/106/45">‘He remembered unto them His covenant and He reversed the decree according to the abundance of His kindness’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And through Thy servants the prophets it is written saying:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="2" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/jeremiah_2_2/jeremiah_2"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/jeremiah_2_2/jeremiah_2/2" n="2"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:jeremiah/2/2">‘Go and proclaim in the ears of Jerusalem saying, <tei:choice><tei:sic>‘Thus</tei:sic><tei:corr>Thus</tei:corr></tei:choice> says the Lord: I remember unto you the grace of your youth, the love of your betrothal, when you followed me in the wilderness in land unsown’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And it was said:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="16" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/ezekiel_16_60/ezekiel_16"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/ezekiel_16_60/ezekiel_16/60" n="60"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:ezekiel/16/60">‘I will remember My covenant with you in the days of your youth and establish with you an everlasting covenant’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>And it was said:  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="31" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/jeremiah_31_19/jeremiah_31"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/musaf/zikhronot_verses/quotes/jeremiah_31_19/jeremiah_31/19" n="19"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:jeremiah/31/19">‘Is Ephraim a dear son to me, or a delightful child that whenever I speak of him, I still remember him? Accordingly, my love for him is aroused, I shall surely have compassion on him, says the Lord’.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
